                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.544/17: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-25T16:00:00+01:00">June 25, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 27—5:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Department’s 45, June 22, 3 p.m. The Foreign Office states that in its
                    opinion article 52 of the Constitution does not give it the right to conclude an
                    international convention depriving Swiss citizens of their nationality. It is
                    preparing a counter-draft looking towards the solution of this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
